Fig. 57.11 The relative sensitivity of various monitoring techniques 
to the occurrence of venous air embolism. BP, Blood pressure; CO, 
cardiac output; CVP, central venous pressure; ECG, electrocardiogram; 
ET-CO2, end-tidal carbon dioxide; PAP, pulmonary artery pressure; 
Stetho, esophageal stethoscope; T-echo, transesophageal echo; VAE, 
venous air embolism.
